# LaTeX build output for research/*.tex — a build product, like dist/ and exports/.
output/

# Third-party prose staged for measurement, never redistributed. `human-excerpts.json` holds
# ~294k words of Mother of Learning and RoyalRoad chapters and this repository is public;
# it is a build product of `taste_calibration.py --dump` over corpora that live on the machine,
# and it regenerates in one command. The *results* files carry only ids and verdicts.
research/quality-measurement/corpora/human-excerpts.json
# Matched-pair benchmark corpus: third-party RoyalRoad and Mother of Learning prose, staged for
# measurement and never redistributed. Same rule as human-excerpts.json above — it is a build
# product of `taste_benchmark.py --build` and regenerates in one command. The committed record is
# the text-free sidecar results/taste-benchmark-corpus.json, which carries every pair's covariates.
research/quality-measurement/corpora/taste-benchmark.json


# Run logs. The JSON and JSONL beside them are the artifacts.
research/quality-measurement/results/*.log

# Residual-stream activation dumps from the latent-taste probe (stage-0 Track P). One vector per
# (text, layer) at 2,560 dims — a few MB, small enough to be tempting, and ignored anyway. Two
# reasons: it is a build product that `latent_probe.py --extract` regenerates from committed
# fixtures in one command, and the moment a family is added whose source is somebody else's prose
# the dump becomes a derived work of a corpus this repository does not own. Deciding that
# case-by-case later is how the 294k near-miss happened (commit bbc6560), so the rule is the same
# for every dump regardless of source. The committed record is the results JSON, which carries
# scene ids, verdicts and provenance and no vectors.
research/quality-measurement/results/*.npz
research/quality-measurement/results/latent-taste-activations*.jsonl

# The book library: reading copies and pastable chapters, republished on every tick and
# resolved beside the database it is derived from. Generated like dist/, and gitignored for
# the same reason — a tree rewritten on every tick would leave the working copy permanently
# dirty for every parallel session sharing this repo. It supersedes exports/, which stays
# ignored above so existing local renders do not suddenly surface in git status.
# NOTES.md is the exception worth knowing about: it is yours, never overwritten, and if you
# want it kept, `git add -f book-library/*/NOTES.md`.
book-library/

# Derived text of third-party prose, produced by the force programme
# (plan/force-program.md §1.6). Continuations sampled from a RoyalRoad seed, retellings in a
# transmission chain and cloze materials cut from an excerpt are all **excerpt-bearing**: a
# continuation carries its seed's register and frequently its sentences, so it falls under the
# same rule that already gitignores the corpora it derives from. Local-only, audited by
# `corpus_leak_audit.py`, regenerable from the pinned families in one command. The committed
# record is `results/force-*.json`, which carries ids, digests and numbers and no prose.
research/quality-measurement/derived/
